{{!-- The front-page wordmark.

     Three parts, set live rather than as an image so it stays sharp on any
     screen, can be selected and read aloud, and recolours itself when the
     masthead is running over a photograph.

       "The"       small, light grey, sitting above and inset from the name
       "A"         carries the rule beneath it — the same mark as the site icon
       "dvisory"   the name proper, in the accent navy
       "Letter"    mid grey, so the eye lands on "Advisory"

     The visually hidden line above it is what a screen reader announces, so
     the decorative split does not reach assistive technology as three
     unrelated fragments. --}}

<span class="tal-wm-vh">{{@site.title}}</span>

<span class="tal-wm" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="tal-wm-the">The</span>
    <span class="tal-wm-name"><span class="tal-wm-a">A</span>dvisory<span class="tal-wm-letter"> Letter</span></span>
</span>
